# R7 stage C allowlist: archive asset paths exempt from manifest-assets.txt
# coverage, one pattern per line (component globs allowed, matched as a
# contiguous path-component subsequence; '#' starts a comment).
#
# Classes exempted here, each backed by source-tree evidence:
# 1. Hadoop-authored webapp UI code (src/main/webapps/<app>/*.{js,html},
#    robots.txt, WEB-INF/web.xml, static helper js/css written by Hadoop).
# 2. Dist-build artifacts: the .gz twins the tarball step creates next to
#    every webapp static file (source tree carries only the plain file).
# 3. Third-party jars' self-description pages (about/license/readme/package
#    .html, jetty-dir.css) — licensed jar-side by their LICENSE-binary entry.
# 4. The YARN API service's webapp marker and the container-executor
#    TERMINAL files not under the curated TERMINAL source path.
# Self-cleaning: an entry that matches no shipped asset fails the gate —
# prune the row when the asset class disappears.
#
# --- 1. Hadoop-authored webapp UI files ---
webapps/*/dfshealth.js
webapps/*/dfshealth.html
webapps/*/explorer.js
webapps/*/explorer.html
webapps/*/federationhealth.js
webapps/*/federationhealth.html
webapps/*/balancer.js
webapps/*/balancer.html
webapps/*/dn.js
webapps/*/datanode.html
webapps/*/snn.js
webapps/*/status.html
webapps/*/jn.js
webapps/*/journalnode.html
webapps/*/robots.txt
webapps/*/index.html
webapps/*/WEB-INF/web.xml
webapps/static/hadoop.css
webapps/static/hadoop.css.gz
webapps/static/dfs-dust.js
webapps/static/rest-csrf.js
webapps/static/json-bignum.js
webapps/static/histogram-hostip.js
webapps/static/rbf.css
webapps/static/busy.gif
webapps/static/index.html
webapps/*/.keep
webapps/api-server/app
webapps/static/federation/federation.js
webapps/static/hadoop-st.png
webapps/static/yarn.css
webapps/static/yarn.dt.plugins.js
webapps/static/dt-sorting/natural.js
# hadoop-common's test jar ships its test webapp stylesheet
webapps/static/test.css
html/showSimulationTrace.html
html/*.template
# --- 1b. the YARN application-catalog WAR's own UI code (Hadoop-authored
# angular app; the WAR's third-party vendor/ tree stays UNEXEMPTED and must
# be covered by manifest-assets.txt) ---
WEB-INF/classes/*.js
js/app.js
js/controllers.js
js/filters.js
js/routes.js
js/services.js
js/bootstrap-hadoop.js
js/bootstrap-hadoop.min.js
css/bootstrap-hadoop.css
css/bootstrap-hadoop.min.css
css/specific.css
css/theme.css
css/img/*
index.html
theme.html
partials/*.html
# --- 2. dist-built gzip twins of webapp static files ---
*.gz
# --- 2b. the release-shaped YARN UIs (-Pyarn-ui): compiled bundle output
# of each module's lock-pinned dependency set (see ui-archive-trees). The
# per-package license statements are the manifest's package-style entries,
# validated against the modules' committed lock files; the bundle files
# themselves (hashed chunks, sourcemaps, compiled css, bundled fonts and
# images, ember/vite build output) are that build's artifacts, not
# individually curated assets. Hadoop-authored support files below.
# A dependency change re-renders these paths but is caught by the lock
# evidence check on the package entries; upstream REMOVING a UI makes
# these rows stale and fails the gate until pruned.
webapps/ui2/assets/*
webapps/ui2/fonts/*
webapps/ui2/config/configs.env
webapps/ui2/crossdomain.xml
webapps/scheduler-ui/assets/*
webapps/scheduler-ui/mock/*
webapps/scheduler-ui/mockServiceWorker.js
webapps/scheduler-ui/favicon.ico
# WAR packaging metadata of the exploded UI WARs (jar-side licensing)
WEB-INF/classes/META-INF/LICENSE.txt
WEB-INF/classes/META-INF/NOTICE.txt
# --- 3. third-party jars' self-description pages ---
about.html
license.html
readme.html
package.html
jetty-dir.css
